2026-08-28T03:20:00Z | PHRASING REFINED, NOT REVERSED | Operator: "I think that WOLF when written next to a name was a rank/role - like a CIT or LIT." He is right and the fix is to my WORDING, not to the substance. f_2345 had said Wolf was "a programme, not a post" -- too sharp a dichotomy, since CIT and LIT are plainly BOTH, each naming a programme and the standing a person holds within it, and each appearing beside a name on these boards exactly as WOLF does. So a Wolf credit IS a designation attached to a person; what the evidence does not support is the ORIGINAL audit reading, that it was a STAFF post alongside Counsellor and Tripper. NOTHING DOWNSTREAM CHANGES: Wolf stays classed as leadership-track alongside CIT/LIT/JC, and the junior-to-staff progression count in f_2335 stays at 44 -- I checked rather than assumed. New source src_oral_aronson_wolf_rank recorded at SECONDARY reliability because the operator hedges it ("I think"), unlike his flat statements on the programme lineage which are primary; the hedge is preserved in the source note and the article footnote rather than being smoothed away. f_2345, wiki/site/named-places-and-camp-vocabulary.md and the build_index.py docstring all updated. KB v5.70 -> v5.71.
