2026-09-05T00:00:00Z  VERIFY/BUILD  A VERIFY pass on oldest-camp-question.md caught an error I introduced earlier the same day, and the check that would have caught it now exists. THE ERROR: when c_061 settled Camp Stephens's wartime closure at 1918, its longest unbroken run was correctly re-dated from 1918-2019 to 1919-2019 -- and the count in front of it was left at "about 102". 1919 to 2019 inclusive is 101. Settling a date and leaving the arithmetic beside it alone is the exact failure this article warns about in other people's records. Corrected in both places it appeared (oldest-camp-question.md and the continuity table in canadian-camping-movement.md), visibly, with a note saying what it said before and why it was wrong. Kanawana's lead is unchanged at roughly 25 seasons -- it was 24 under the wrong figure. THE CHECK: scripts/verify/consistency.py gains a third rule class, SPAN -- "N seasons, YYYY-YYYY" must satisfy N == end - start + 1. General, no registry, like the TABLE rule. SEASONS AND SUMMERS ONLY, never "years": a season count is inclusive of both ends, while "37 years (1919-1956)" is an elapsed duration and correct as written, and both readings occur in this wiki. An approximation marker (about, roughly, ~) allows a tolerance of 2, since "about 87 seasons" over an unpinned span is an honest statement rather than an arithmetic claim. Probed against the whole wiki before wiring in: three hits, all three "years" false positives, which is why the rule excludes that word; six genuine season-span statements are now checked. Verified by restoring the bad figure deliberately -- it reports 'wiki/history/oldest-camp-question.md:396 "**102 seasons** (1919-2019" -- 102 seasons stated, but 1919 to 2019 inclusive is 101' and exits 1. The rest of the VERIFY pass on oldest-camp-question.md was clean: 70 fact references all resolve, footnote markers 1-19 and source entries 1-19 correspond exactly, every src_ id exists, and sources_cited matched the text; one fact reference (f_4839) was missing from kb_facts_used and is added. All six verify scripts pass.
